From e9baa2f730d3f274ce3eacec3c34e187490dd647 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rpiios <grinkod.bogdan@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:47:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Raspberry Pi 3: SD multi-block read-ahead; mouse layout from
 HID report descriptor

Fourth real-hardware boot (watchdog): not hung but slow. The SD driver
was busy ~98% of the time at about 0.85 MB/s, one CMD17 per 512-byte
sector, while dyld reads the ~300 MB shared cache. And the mouse
ignored SET_PROTOCOL(boot): its reports carry 16-bit X/Y in bytes 4-7,
so reading boot-layout bytes 1-2 never moved the cursor.

- rpi3_sd: on a miss, read a run of sectors with one CMD18 (auto CMD12)
  into a 128 KB buffer; the run doubles from 16 to 256 sectors while
  reads stay sequential. Writes invalidate it; after three CMD18
  failures fall back to single blocks for good.
- rpi3_usb: fetch the mouse interface's HID report descriptor and find
  buttons, X and Y (offset, size, report id, relative/absolute); keep
  report protocol. Boot protocol only if the descriptor cannot be used.
- rpi3_touch: 16-bit deltas scaled to 0.25 px per count; absolute
  pointers mapped onto the screen.
---
